# backtest-overfitting

[![CI](https://github.com/vendraholdings/backtest-overfitting/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/vendraholdings/backtest-overfitting/actions/workflows/ci.yml)

Overfitting diagnostics applied to a complete search of <<n_trials>> machine-learning configurations for a cross-sectional equity strategy.
The best configuration has a net Sharpe ratio of <<best_sr>>; the question is how much of that survives selection bias.

> **Scope.** The trials were run on today's index members. A later point-in-time rerun in the
> [quant](https://github.com/vendraholdings/quant) repository shows that the family-level signal is largely survivorship
> bias. This project measures a separate effect, selection bias from searching many configurations, and its diagnostics
> apply unchanged to any trial matrix.

![Joint density of in-sample and out-of-sample rank, rotating view](docs/hero.gif)

*Figure 3. Joint density of the in-sample and out-of-sample rank of every trial over <<n_splits>> cross-validation splits (log base 2, relative to independence).
An interactive version is on the [project page](https://vendraholdings.github.io/backtest-overfitting/).*

## Results

| Quantity | Value |
|---|---|
| Best net Sharpe ratio among <<n_trials>> trials (mean of all trials: <<mean_sr>>) | <<best_sr>> |
| Haircut Sharpe ratio after Bonferroni / Holm adjustment for <<n_trials>> tests | <<hc_bonf>> |
| Deflated Sharpe ratio of the best trial | <<dsr>> |
| Probability of backtest overfitting (CSCV, S = 16, <<n_splits>> splits) | <<pbo>> |
| Out-of-sample Sharpe ratio: selected trial / average trial | <<oos_sel>> / <<oos_avg>> |

The trials share one signal. All of them are profitable, and White's Reality Check and Hansen's SPA test reject the null of no skill (p <<p_spa>>).
The choice among them is not informative: the configuration with the best in-sample Sharpe ratio (<<is_sel>> on average) has an out-of-sample Sharpe ratio of <<oos_sel>>,
no higher than that of an average configuration. Searching more configurations raised the best reported Sharpe ratio only from <<curve_best_10>> (10 trials) to <<curve_best_all>>.
The trial universe uses current index members, so absolute levels are overstated; the results concern selection, not tradable performance.
Every number above is generated by the code in this repository and quoted, with its method, in the [paper](paper/paper.pdf).

* **Live page:** <https://vendraholdings.github.io/backtest-overfitting/>
* **Paper:** [`paper/paper.pdf`](paper/paper.pdf) (8 pages)

## Methods

| Method | Reference |
|---|---|
| Probability of backtest overfitting by combinatorially symmetric cross-validation (exact, one matrix product) | Bailey, Borwein, López de Prado and Zhu (2017) |
| Probabilistic and deflated Sharpe ratio, minimum track record length | Bailey and López de Prado (2012, 2014) |
| Effective number of trials: eigenvalue, clustering and simulated-null calibration | this repository |
| Bonferroni, Holm and BHY Sharpe haircuts | Harvey and Liu (2015) |
| Reality Check and SPA test with the stationary bootstrap (<<n_boot>> resamples) | White (2000); Hansen (2005); Politis and Romano (1994) |
| Monte Carlo validation with planted signals | this repository |

Validation: CSCV is compared with a loop implementation, the deflated Sharpe ratio with an independent implementation (agreement to 1e-13), the SPA test with the `arch` package, and
all diagnostics on synthetic trials with a known answer (paper, Section 4).

## Reproduce

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). The trial returns (`data/trials.parquet`, <<n_periods>> periods by <<n_trials>> trials) are included, so the price data are not needed.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vendraholdings/backtest-overfitting
cd backtest-overfitting
make all        # tests, results (about 70 s), figures, paper, README and site
make serve      # http://localhost:8000
```

`make all` also renders the hero animation, which needs `ffmpeg` only for the MP4 file. `scripts/export_trials.py` documents how the return matrix was rebuilt from the original per-trial predictions.

## Layout

```
overfit/    cscv.py  sharpe.py  haircut.py  spa.py  trials.py  validate.py  synthetic.py  plots.py  facts.py
scripts/    export_trials.py  run_all.py  make_figures.py  make_hero.py  build_paper.py  build_readme.py
tests/      CSCV vs slow loop, PSR/DSR closed forms, haircuts, bootstrap, SPA, synthetic validation
site/       build.py  (static page; Plotly bundled)
paper/      paper.typ.tmpl  refs.bib  paper.pdf  figures/  (light, for the paper)
docs/       hero.gif  hero.mp4  figures/  (dark, for the README and site)
data/       trials.parquet  configs.parquet
results/    summary.json and tables
```

